            "block_id": "/page/0/Text/16",
            "page": 0,
            "study_index": 1,
            "granularity": "paragraph",
            "quote": "[/page/0/Text/16] Among early adolescents in the United States (U.S.), the prevalence of cigarette smoking is at its lowest level in recent decades. Nonetheless, given the risks of smoking in early development, it remains critically important to study both risk factors for smoking and risks from smoking. This longitudinal study with U.S. early adolescents examines smoking initiation and tests a model of reciprocal prediction between ever smoking and the personality trait of urgency (i.e., mood-based impulsivity), a trait that increases risk for multiple forms of dysfunction.",
            "bbox": null
          }
        ],
